  "answer": "The goal was not met. Three settings cleared the bar, each on a different scene: 096988dd with the cars at 0 s and 2x speed (S5), and 023b7fcc and 09a95ffa with the cars at 0 s and 1.25x speed (S1, S6). Only S1 is clearly the policy's fault: the ego sped up and steered left into a car in the next lane. At S6 a replayed car overtaking from behind clipped the ego while it held its lane, so the policy's fault is unclear. At S5 most failures come from a bad track for actor 9, which appears overlapping the ego at handoff, not from a driving mistake. So only one of the three is a clean policy failure. A fourth scene, 19f339ba, fails often at 1.25x but has not cleared the bar. There the policy drifts left even though its route command says RIGHT (S18, S19), so its left drift still causes collisions at 2 Hz. The study only tried shifts of \u00b10.5 s and speeds of 1.25x to 2x, never a recorded-timing run on the same replay setup, so it does not show whether the retiming causes these failures.",
